.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
.TH PKGMK.CONF 5 "" "imai #VERSION#" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
pkgmk.conf \- executable configuration for pkgmk
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pkgmk
parses command-line options first, then sources the current directory's Pkgfile
followed by /etc/pkgmk.conf. Recipe and configuration assignments can override
command-line settings; for example, PKGMK_NO_STRIP=no in configuration overrides
\-ns. An alternative configuration file is selected with
.BR "pkgmk \-cf" .
Assignments, arrays, shell functions and other Bash syntax are supported.
Configuration is trusted executable Bash running with the caller's privileges,
including root; it is not sandboxed. Shell state and function overrides persist
through the build controller. See pkgfile(5) for the recipe boundary.
.SH VARIABLES
Defaults below are internal defaults before the recipe and configuration run.
The shipped configuration additionally exports CFLAGS and CXXFLAGS with
-O2 -march=x86-64 -pipe. Compiler flags do not establish support for untested
architectures.
.TP
.B CFLAGS, CXXFLAGS, LDFLAGS
Export compiler and linker flags for build tools that honor them.
.TP
.B JOBS, MAKEFLAGS
Optional parallel-build settings. JOBS alone has no universal effect; set
MAKEFLAGS or use JOBS in the recipe as needed.
.TP
.B PKGMK_SOURCE_MIRRORS
Bash array of source mirror URLs, tried in order before the original URL.
Default: empty array.
.TP
.B PKGMK_SOURCE_DIR
Directory for downloaded sources. Default: directory of Pkgfile.
.TP
.B PKGMK_PACKAGE_DIR
Directory for built packages. Default: directory of Pkgfile.
.TP
.B PKGMK_WORK_DIR
Working directory containing src and pkg staging directories.
Default: work below the directory of Pkgfile. Configure only a directory
whose contents may be removed by pkgmk.
.TP
.B PKGMK_TMPFS
Set to yes to require executable, writable tmpfs for work. Default: no.
With the final PKGMK_WORK_DIR equal to the default, pkgmk reserves
/var/tmp/pkgmk/<recipe name> and mounts tmpfs there, containing src and pkg.
Explicitly assigning the default has the same effect. The parent is created mode0700 when absent and must otherwise be a
root-owned mode0700 directory. Unknown existing work directories are never adopted.
Recipe names must be nonempty single path components other than dot, dot-dot or .state.
The protected .state directory stores permanent per-recipe ownership locks and
mount provenance. Locks are held throughout each managed build.
Successful builds and signature, MD5 or footprint check failures release managed
work by ordinary unmount and directory removal unless keep-work is selected.
A footprint check failure leaves the generated package intact. Recipe or extraction
failures, interruption and extract-only retain work and print its location. Busy mounts are retained with failure status;
pkgmk never forces or lazily detaches them. A subsequent build replaces
inactive retained work only after its controller exited normally and its recorded
ownership, unique mount identity, boot and mount namespace match. Active builds
are refused without waiting. Recovery requires kernel unique mount-ID support
(Linux6.8 or newer); ordinary managed builds do not. Untracked mounts, interrupted
controllers, native-parent crashes and work retained by version0.1.3 require
separately approved manual cleanup.
Mounting requires appropriate privileges.
A nondefault work path retains the existing cleanup behavior and must be on tmpfs;
pkgmk does not mount or unmount it. There is no disk fallback. Source downloads,
finished packages and TMPDIR remain unchanged. Tmpfs can swap, fill up and
disappear at reboot; this option is not a build sandbox or a capacity guarantee.
.TP
.B PKGMK_LOG_DIR
Existing directory for a unique mode0600 recipe log. Empty by default (disabled).
Relative paths are resolved against the original Pkgfile directory. Only the
first recipe capture per controller is logged; nested and later captures warn
and skip a separate log. Nested output can appear in the enclosing log.
Ordinary recursive child processes have independent logs. The path is printed
at capture start. Logs are retained without rotation, including incomplete logs.
Setup and write failures warn and disable the sink without changing recipe status.
Only the default build callback is captured, not downloads, extraction, stripping,
packaging or installation. Configured callback replacements remain authoritative.
Stdout and stderr remain live and separate; the log merges their observed bytes
without guaranteeing cross-stream ordering. Logging uses pipes and can change
application buffering, color and terminal detection. Logs include shell trace
and can expose credentials. Capture ends at recipe completion; detached writers
are not awaited and may encounter closed pipes at invocation exit.
.TP
.B PKGMK_BUILD_TIME
Set to yes to report monotonic elapsed seconds for every recipe callback,
including failures. Default: no. Independent of logging; other build phases and
skipped builds are not timed. Clock or reporting failures must not change the
recipe result. No timing history is retained.
.TP
.B PKGMK_DOWNLOAD_PROG
Downloader: curl (default), GNU-compatible wget or aria2c.
Aria2c defaults to 4 connections per server, 4 splits, a 20 MiB minimum split
size, 15-second connection timeout and 60-second timeout, with 3 attempts
and a 3-second retry delay. It does not load aria2.conf.
BusyBox wget is explicitly rejected because it lacks required options.
.TP
.B PKGMK_CURL_OPTS, PKGMK_WGET_OPTS, PKGMK_ARIA2_OPTS
Additional arguments for the corresponding downloader, split on shell whitespace
without globbing. Embedded quote characters are not reinterpreted as shell
quoting. Default: empty.
.TP
.B PKGMK_DOWNLOAD
Set to yes to download missing remote sources. Default: no.
.TP
.B PKGMK_IGNORE_SIGNATURE
Set to yes to disable port signature checks. Default: no.
If a signature is absent, the ordinary workflow can fall back to legacy MD5
checking; absence is not authenticated provenance.
.TP
.B PKGMK_IGNORE_MD5SUM
Set to yes to disable legacy MD5 checks. Default: no.
.TP
.B PKGMK_IGNORE_FOOTPRINT
Set to yes to disable footprint checks. Default: no.
.TP
.B PKGMK_IGNORE_NEW
Set to yes to tolerate new footprint entries. Default: no.
.TP
.B PKGMK_NO_STRIP
Set to yes to retain unstripped binaries and libraries. Default: no.
.TP
.B PKGMK_COMPRESSION_MODE
Package compression: gz (default), bz2, xz, lz or zst. Requires bsdtar
support for the selected codec.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
export CFLAGS='-O2 -march=x86-64 -pipe'
export CXXFLAGS="$CFLAGS"
export MAKEFLAGS='-j2'
PKGMK_SOURCE_MIRRORS=(https://mirror.example.invalid/sources)
PKGMK_COMPRESSION_MODE=zst
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/pkgmk.conf
Default global build configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkgfile (5),
.BR pkgmk (8),
.BR bash (1)
.SH COPYRIGHT
